o":"Mr. Michael J. Saylor | Executive Chairman | Age 60 | Compensation: $780,732 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $315K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers. Stock-based compensation of $35K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Strategy Inc is a large-cap technology business with a $54.6B market cap on $477M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at -10% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 79% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $75M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -117.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 29.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 1148% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"